      "text": "How ice grows · deposition\nThree reference frames\n01\nAn existing crystal\n\nIce is already present. Hollow rings trace invisible water vapor.\n\n02\nVapor adds to ice\n\nDeposition changes water directly from gas to solid.\n\n03\nA larger crystal\n\nAdded water builds the ice. Liquid droplets can still coexist nearby.\n\nRead left to right, or top to bottom. Shapes and timing are illustrative. Below 0°C, some droplets may remain liquid (supercooled)."
